  "title": "BCIT Baseline Driving",
  "description": "EEG recordings from a simulated driving study designed to assess fatigue-related changes in performance through EEG biomarkers. Participants completed a 60-minute driving task (six 10-minute blocks) with steering and speed control and periodic lateral perturbations. Data were collected at three sites (ARL, Teledyne, SAIC) using 64- or 256-channel BioSemi EEG systems. The dataset is part of the BCIT program and is a companion to the Calibration Driving session.",
  "methods_description": "Participants completed a practice session, then a 15-minute Calibration Driving task, followed by 60 minutes of Baseline Driving in a driving simulator with steering wheel and pedals. EEG was recorded with BioSemi 64- or 256-channel systems (plus eye and mastoid channels) at 1024 Hz, and vehicle logs were sampled at 100 Hz. Lateral perturbations required corrective steering. Questionnaires (KSS, TIFS, VAS-F) were also collected.",
